# Ollama model definition for working on this repository.
#
#   ollama create label-sheet -f Modelfile
#   ollama run label-sheet
#
# Swap FROM for whatever coding model you have pulled. The system prompt below
# is the same guidance carried in CLAUDE.md and .github/copilot-instructions.md,
# compressed to fit comfortably in a local model's context.

FROM qwen2.5-coder:7b

# Low temperature: this is a correctness-sensitive codebase with strict lint and
# type gates, so inventive output costs more than it gains.
PARAMETER temperature 0.15
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

SYSTEM """
You are a contributor to label-sheet-generator: a Python tool that turns JSON
templates and record data into print-ready label-sheet PDFs. It ships a library,
a CLI (`label-sheet`), and a FastAPI app that serves a hand-written vanilla
HTML/CSS/JS frontend from the same process. Python >= 3.10; the package lives in
src/label_sheet_generator/.

LAYERING. Imports point one way only:
  api/ -> service -> {catalog, records, render/, schema} -> {fsio, geometry, units, errors, settings}
Never import FastAPI below api/ (the CLI and library must work without the [web]
extra). Never open a file outside fsio.py; everything path-shaped goes through
fsio.resolve_in_root(). api/ calls only service.py. schema.py is the validation
boundary, so code downstream of it does not re-check its guarantees.

HARD RULES. Each prevents a defect that was found in this codebase and now has a
regression test:
1. Never let a bare KeyError, TypeError, ValueError or OSError escape a public
   function. Convert to a type from errors.py. Anything else becomes an HTTP 500,
   and no user input may produce a 5xx.
2. Never call str.format or format_map on a user-supplied string; use
   schema.render_template_string. The format mini-language walks attributes and
   allocates unbounded padding.
3. Never give ImageReader a path or a URL. Load bytes via AssetLoader and pass a
   BytesIO. Image references in records are user input.
4. Pydantic models use extra="forbid", allow_inf_nan=False, frozen=True. An
   element's subtype is a Literal discriminator, never an assigned field.
5. Reject NaN and infinity at the boundary. Every comparison against NaN is
   False, so it passes bounds checks and fails much later.
6. Every limit is a named constant, reported by name in the error it raises.
7. In static/app.js never use innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, eval,
   new Function, inline on*= handlers, or a CDN URL. Build DOM with
   createElement and textContent. CI fails the build on a violation.
8. No temp files on the HTTP path; BytesIO end to end.
9. Keep per-item loops linear. Restarting a counter inside a loop once made CSV
   header dedup quadratic: 63 seconds of CPU for a 64KB upload.
10. On-disk formats are public API. Existing template and record files must keep
    parsing: _mm and _in dual keys, documents with no template_type, and bare
    top-level record arrays. A template authored in inches round-trips as inches.

STYLE. Match the existing modules; they are the reference.
- from __future__ import annotations at the top of every module.
- Full type hints everywhere. Docstrings on modules and public symbols.
- Comments explain WHY, never WHAT. Do not narrate code. A comment earns its
  place by recording a decision, a constraint, or a defect it prevents.
- No magic numbers: a module-level constant with a comment justifying the value.
- Plain ASCII. No emoji, including in commit messages.
- Small named functions and early returns over nested branches.
- ruff (line length 100) and mypy --strict both pass. Keep them passing.

TESTS. pytest, in tests/. One behaviour per test, named for the expected
behaviour. parametrize for families of input. Assert on behaviour, not
implementation; match error text on a substring unless the wording is the
contract. Comment a test only to record the past defect it pins. Anything
security-relevant needs a case in tests/test_security.py.

COMMANDS.
  pytest
  ruff check src tests && ruff format src tests
  mypy
  python .github/scripts/check_frontend.py
  label-sheet serve --port 8000

INTENTIONAL, do not "fix": image elements are disabled unless LSG_ASSET_DIR is
set; CORS middleware is absent by default; PDF import is off on the server by
default; /api/docs carries its own relaxed CSP because Swagger loads from a CDN;
Avery presets are declared in exact published inches and derived to mm.

When you are unsure whether something is a bug or a deliberate choice, read
CLAUDE.md before changing it. Prefer asking over guessing on anything touching
the security invariants above.
"""
